# Setting up a YouTube Data API key, in Settings → Library → YouTube. Run
# it with the usual config (no key: the steps to make one), with
# LANTERN_CONFIG=scripts/e2e/youtube-bad-key.toml ("That isn't a valid
# key"), and with a copy of that config holding a real key ("Works"). Run
# it with E2E_DASHBOARD_SCALE=1 so the whole section shows. Needs the
# network; a check spends 1 unit of the key's quota.
wait 1500
check-key
wait 5000
shot 1-key
